[method]
The paper used a whole-mouse-brain ThICK immunostaining workflow built around iDISCO-BABB solvent clearing. Commercially available primary antibodies were chemically stabilized into SPEARs, applied to cleared mouse brains, and imaged volumetrically with SPIM and two-photon tomography. The workflow included image processing for spot detection, tractography, digital removal of intravascular SPEAR precipitates, and benchmarking against optimized conventional immunostaining, CUBIC-HistoVIsion, and iDISCO. This relates to the proposed method because the plan uses iDISCO clearing followed by MesoSPIM imaging to map axons; the paper demonstrates an iDISCO-BABB-based clearing and SPIM imaging pipeline and evaluates iDISCO as a baseline for deep immunolabeling, although it adds SPEARs and ThICK rather than relying on standard iDISCO alone.
[results]
The supplied excerpt contains section headings but no numerical results, so specific quantitative outcomes, statistical significance, and baseline comparisons cannot be reported. It indicates that the paper performed stringent benchmarking of immunolabeling depths and compared ThICK/SPEARs with iDISCO and CUBIC-HistoVIsion, and that it quantified intravascular SPEAR precipitates, but no depth values, spot counts, or significance values are available in the provided text.
[context]
Experimental context was whole mouse brain tissue processed with iDISCO-BABB clearing and imaged by SPIM and two-photon tomography. The method included controls for intravascular antibody precipitates and benchmarking against iDISCO and CUBIC-HistoVIsion. The excerpt does not specify the number of brains, antibody targets, voxel size, imaging resolution, or statistical tests. For the proposed plan, the relevant constraint is that iDISCO clearing can support whole-brain SPIM imaging, but the paper’s benchmarking suggests that deep immunolabeling performance should be evaluated against iDISCO baselines and may require additional stabilization or optimized staining for deep axonal labeling.
[end related work 3]

