[method]
The paper used a brain-wide complete-morphology pipeline to compare projection patterns across defined neuron types. Whole mouse brains were cleared and immunolabeled, imaged with MesoSPIM, registered to the Allen CCF, and complete neuronal morphologies were reconstructed. Axonal arbors were then partitioned into CCF brain regions to create categorical region-wise projection profiles, and these profiles were used to cluster and compare projection patterns across cortical, thalamic, and striatal neuron types, including cortical L2/3, L4, L5 IT, L5 ET, Car3, thalamic core/matrix, and striatal MSN types. For example, cortical axon arbors of core-type thalamic neurons were clustered by their CCF-region profiles, and individual 3D projection maps were compared with mesoscale population-level projection maps for thalamic nuclei. This is directly analogous to the proposed method's categorical brain-region analysis and spatial comparison of 3D projection maps, although the paper compares neuron types and single-neuron versus population maps rather than genetically defined SSp-bfd versus SSs injections.
[results]
The paper reports reconstruction of 1,000 complete neurons from 10 mouse brains. The region-wise arbor analysis identified distinct projection profiles for the listed neuron types and revealed topographic organization in long-range projections, especially for core-type thalamic neurons. Single-neuron thalamic projection maps were consistent with population-level projection patterns for nuclei such as VPM, showing overlapping target regions while preserving neuron-specific differences. The provided excerpt does not report numerical correlation coefficients, effect sizes, or p-values for the cross-class or single-versus-population projection comparisons.
[context]
The experiments used whole mouse brains, iDISCO immunolabeling/clearing, MesoSPIM imaging at approximately 5 µm near-isotropic resolution, and registration to the Allen CCF. Sparse labeling of projection neuron types was used, and analysis relied on mBrainAnalyzer and Neuron-beta-style reconstruction and arbor partitioning into CCF regions. The paper's population is not whisker-specific SSp-bfd/SSs, and it does not include the proposed TrailMap-based axon segmentation, injection-site normalization, or optogenetic functional validation; it therefore serves as a methodological precedent for brain-wide projection quantification and categorical/spatial comparison of projection maps.
[end related work 2]

